:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:23:24-07:00","id":1198404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198401#post1198401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only got into Magic with original Zendikar, so all the nostalgia in Dominaria is wasted on me, but I\u2019m pleasantly surprised by the increase in story quality under this new author. Still hoping we can return to Tarkir soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want Tarkir to be added to Areana. I've been playing since Weatherlight, so the nostalgia is <b>strong</b> with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:24:33-07:00","id":1198405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198404#post1198404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want Tarkir to be added to Areana. I've been playing since Weatherlight, so the nostalgia is <b>strong</b> with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep up with the cards, but don\u2019t play; the story and art is most of why I\u2019m here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:30:31-07:00","id":1198407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198405#post1198405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I keep up with the cards, but don\u2019t play; the story and art is most of why I\u2019m here.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the funny thing is that this has been my prime motivator too, which is one of the reasons I haven't cared lately. The story hasn't been grabbing me as much. I'm hoping it starts to pick up again. But I do enjoy playing the game a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:42:32-07:00","id":1198410,"title":"","content":"Dominaria is fascinating to me, because while I dabbled with Magic as early on as Portal, I got seriously into the game with Time Spiral Block, which was the <i>first</i> let\u2019s-go-back-to-Dominaria nostalgia block. So, it\u2019s neat seeing that happen again, and how they\u2019re approaching it differently this time. Also, starting off in what is still widely considered the best Standard environment of all time may have spoiled me a bit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am super excited for Arena, because I still adore Magic, but I just can\u2019t afford to play it competitively any more, and playing casually is just not as satisfying for me. It\u2019ll be great to be able to play magic at least semi-competitively without having to spend money on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:44:18-07:00","id":1198411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198410#post1198410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, I am super excited for Arena, because I still adore Magic, but I just can\u2019t afford to play it competitively any more, and playing casually is just not as satisfying for me. It\u2019ll be great to be able to play magic at least semi-competitively without having to spend money on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, word for word.<br /> <br /> I also keep up with the game because of story and curiosity for the cards, but haven't bought one in a long while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:09:17-07:00","id":1198416,"title":"","content":"I'm the exact opposite. I love deckbuilding, but I've always played casually. I enjoy the tactics, I just never could get into the competitive scene and prefer things like EDH or pauper. Plus the world building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:20:37-07:00","id":1198419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198416#post1198416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm the exact opposite. I love deckbuilding, but I've always played casually. I enjoy the tactics, I just never could get into the competitive scene and prefer things like EDH or pauper. Plus the world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s funny you mention the competitive <i>scene</i>, because that\u2019s another part of why Arena appeals to me. While I love playing Magic competitively, I hate the competitive Magic scene. While money is what keeps me from going back to paper magic, the tournament environment was what drove me away in the first place. It\u2019s mostly fine, but a few bad apples can ruin the whole experience, and in a community as insular as the Denver MtG tournament circuit, it\u2019s impossible to avoid those bad apples.<br /> <br /> But once you go Spike, you never go back, at least in my experience. Every time I\u2019ve tried to play Magic casually since building my first top tier deck, all I see are the problems with my build, and the potential to make it better. The only way I\u2019ve been able to play casually is by creating artificial restrictions for myself and building the most competitive deck I can within those limitations. And still it just feels like \u201cthis could be better.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-22-2018, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:55:36-07:00","id":1198437,"title":"","content":"I have a love/hate relationship with Magic. I love the game, but I hate having to buy new cards every block or so to be allowed in the gamestore games. Back at my last duty station, us grognards would play casually every game day before the RPG of the day. <br /> <br /> Now it's almost impossible to find a casual player where I am currently living. The RPG gamers I know don't want to invest in the cards, and the card players don't want to play RPGs or will only play D&amp;D 5th ed.<br /> <br /> <br /> I bought into the game back in the Beta block. I used to buy a booster or two every payday, so now I have a somewhat large collection of cards that I can't use in official play because they are too old. But I keep them in the hopes that one day, I'll find some mugs to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:08:13-07:00","id":1198442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198437#post1198437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a love/hate relationship with Magic. I love the game, but I hate having to buy new cards every block or so to be allowed in the gamestore games. Back at my last duty station, us grognards would play casually every game day before the RPG of the day. <br /> <br /> Now it's almost impossible to find a casual player where I am currently living. The RPG gamers I know don't want to invest in the cards, and the card players don't want to play RPGs or will only play D&amp;D 5th ed.<br /> <br /> <br /> I bought into the game back in the Beta block. I used to buy a booster or two every payday, so now I have a somewhat large collection of cards that I can't use in official play because they are too old. But I keep them in the hopes that one day, I'll find some mugs to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you heard of Legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:16:38-07:00","id":1198445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread#post1198398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any questions about Arena?</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a basic question, but... who are your opponents? Are you randomly paired against other players online? Is there any sort of skill-based matchmaking involved? Can set up matches against friends or other specific users? Can you play against AI opponents? And is it all one on one or is there any multiplayer support?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:27:54-07:00","id":1198449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198445#post1198445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a basic question, but... who are your opponents? Are you randomly paired against other players online? Is there any sort of skill-based matchmaking involved? Can set up matches against friends or other specific users? Can you play against AI opponents? And is it all one on one or is there any multiplayer support?</div> </div> </div> </div>Random pairing for now. Currently there is only an option to play Constructed Duels. There are rankings and I expect that it influences the matchmaking process, but I have no idea how. I'd wager good money that multiplayer (and hopefully Commander) are coming down the pipe, but that the format is limited to Constructed currently to focus the Beta. No idea about playing against AI, but it's not a bad idea for testing decks. I also really liked the skill challenges in Duels, so that would be a neat way to earn extra gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:54:51-07:00","id":1198540,"title":"","content":"I started playing when I was in middle school back in '99 and had at one time collected/read nearly all of the novels. I've been in and out of the game over the years, with my last real stint being during Return to Ravnica (which was interesting because I wasn't actually playing during the first Ravnica). I'm pretty grognard-y with regard to most of the current lore, but I didn't think that Dominaria would actually hit my nostalgia buttons all that hard.<br /> <br /> I was <i>incorrect</i>.<br /> <br /> Just seeing Karn, Teferi, and Jhoira in the promo banner took me back to being eleven years old reading Time Streams in the basement of a church where the other kids didn't understand why I enjoyed books and the adults just watched CMT all day. If that image seems weirdly detailed and personal to you its because I'm probably going to be spending some money in the near future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:09:45-07:00","id":1198547,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, Brawl looks like a genuinely awesome format. I hope Arena has support for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T03:31:14-07:00","id":1198601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198442#post1198442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you heard of Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have heard of it, it just doesn't seem to be in use in the shops close to me. Standard and Sealed Drafts are the popular formats here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:58:42-07:00","id":1198836,"title":"","content":"Just for fun, since it tends to lead to entertaining discussions: best and worst Planeswalker? <br /> <br /> Vraska's my favorite, both for the character and because I tend to gravitate towards Black/Green decks quite frequently. Sarkhan and Kiora, aka the Dragon &amp; Monsters from the Depth fan, deserve a honorable mention, because I totally get them. <br /> <br /> On the other side, Garruk's bores me to no end.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T15:12:46-07:00","id":1198861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1198836#post1198836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, since it tends to lead to entertaining discussions: best and worst Planeswalker? <br /> <br /> Vraska's my favorite, both for the character and because I tend to gravitate towards Black/Green decks quite frequently. Sarkhan and Kiora, aka the Dragon &amp; Monsters from the Depth fan, deserve a honorable mention, because I totally get them. <br /> <br /> On the other side, Garruk's bores me to no end.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I assume from your answer you mean in terms of which of the characters do we like the most/least. I haven\u2019t really kept up with the story after Return to Ravnica, so I don\u2019t know if more recent events might change my opinion, but I always liked Liliana. I\u2019m a fan of those edgy characters who\u2019s loyalties are always a little unclear, I love the witch in over her head trying to play multiple patrons against each other angle. I like necromancers. I got the implication from her transforming Legendary Creature card that she got into necromancy through a desire to heal, which is always cool. And her name is an anagram for \u201ca villainess\u201d which is cute. Honorable mentions to Elspeth because who doesn\u2019t love badass lady knights, and Chandra because who doesn\u2019t love badass lady pyromancers.<br /> <br /> Least favorite... Probably Gideon. He\u2019s boring, he stole the iconic white planeswalker spotlight from Ajani who was much more interesting, and I <i>think</i> he started the Gatewatch, which I don\u2019t care for. Dishonorable mentions to Nicol Bolas for being a one-note villain and Tezeret and Sarkhan Vol for being his minions.<br /> <br /> I also feel super conflicted about Teferi and Venser. Two of my favorite characters during the Time Spiral story, before Planeswalker was a card type, both of whom came back (or will be coming back in Teferi\u2019s case) as blue white Planeswalker cards, despite that not making sense in either case - Venser has the spark but Teferi sensed that there was something different about it and thought it was probably not able to ignite, which I am willing to forgive as it was clearly foreshadowing neowalkers. But Teferi gave up his own spark to stop the Time Spiral cataclysm from ripping the multiverse apart. They\u2019re going to need a damn good explanation for why he\u2019s a Planeswalker again to not cheapen that sacrifice, and not some nonsense like Nicol Bolas doing... whatever he did in the Alara Malestrom.<br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of characters from Dominaria, I might want to change my answer for favorite to Karn. Part of the Legacy Weapon, a golem with the spark, a pacifist, created Mirrodin... Yeah, he\u2019s my favorite Planeswalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-0