key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T08:42:30-07:00","id":1310040,"title":"","content":"I just bought myself stuff to make a budget Xantcha, Sleeper Agent Commander deck, and I\u2019m super excited for it. It\u2019s been a long time since I\u2019ve played paper Magic, and I\u2019ve missed it. Plus Xantcha looks like a really fun political commander that will make games really interesting even if I\u2019m not winning, which is a good place to be in with a budget deck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T13:12:14-07:00","id":1310095,"title":"","content":"Just found out about the new \u201cLondon Mulligain\u201d rule they tested at the Mythic Championship. Hoping they decide to go with it, because it sounds way better than the Paris or Vancouver mulligain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T08:50:58-07:00","id":1314302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1310040#post1310040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just bought myself stuff to make a budget Xantcha, Sleeper Agent Commander deck, and I\u2019m super excited for it. It\u2019s been a long time since I\u2019ve played paper Magic, and I\u2019ve missed it. Plus Xantcha looks like a really fun political commander that will make games really interesting even if I\u2019m not winning, which is a good place to be in with a budget deck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Xantcha is one of my favorite characters from back when I was really into the novels, so I've been interested getting a copy just for that reason alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T11:47:57-07:00","id":1314329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1314302#post1314302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xantcha is one of my favorite characters from back when I was really into the novels, so I've been interested getting a copy just for that reason alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The card looks really fun for multiplayer. My vorthos side also loves how well she synergizes with Heartstone.<br /> <br /> On another note, I recently found out that <a href=\"https://mtg.gamepedia.com/Oathbreaker\" target=\"_blank\">Oathbreaker</a><br /> is a thing, and I really want to try it. Teferi is my favorite character, and I\u2019d love to make a deck around one of his planeswalker cards (even if I am still a little annoyed that they cheapened his sacrifice at the end of the Time Spiral story by giving him his spark back the very next time the story went back to Dominaria.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-25-2019, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T09:30:07-07:00","id":1326286,"title":"","content":"Anyone know a way to git gud at this game that isn't boring and I can do while doing chores and stuff? As those who say my post in the You Know What I Hate Thread know, I suck at this game despite playing for years and it's less effort to just get good enough to win ocassionally without a mana-screwed opponent than to sell off all my cards and find a new way to spend my weekends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T22:05:10-07:00","id":1326613,"title":"","content":"<b>New MtG set art drops</b><br /> <br /> That high pitch squealing you hear is all the Changeling writers and fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T09:18:41-07:00","id":1326731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1326286#post1326286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know a way to git gud at this game that isn't boring and I can do while doing chores and stuff? As those who say my post in the You Know What I Hate Thread know, I suck at this game despite playing for years and it's less effort to just get good enough to win ocassionally without a mana-screwed opponent than to sell off all my cards and find a new way to spend my weekends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty decent at the game (I\u2019m no pro or anything, but I can hold my own at FNM.) I could probably give you some pointers, but it would help to know more specifically what you struggle with.<br /> <br /> One of the most common problems people who struggle with the game have is that they overvalue certain things (e.g. protecting their life total at all costs instead of treating it as a resource) and undervalue others (e.g. not understanding the importance of tempo and/or card advantage), which causes them to make poor deckbuilding decisions and evaluate board states poorly.<br /> <br /> The best way to improve, in my experience, is to play with more skilled opponents (or watch them play, if you don\u2019t have the ability to play against them yourself) and pay close attention to the way they play, especially when they make decisions that seem strange to you. Look at top-tier deck lists, proxy them, and play with them to figure out what makes them tick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:47:12-07:00","id":1326823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1326731#post1326731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way to improve, in my experience, is to play with more skilled opponents (or watch them play, if you don\u2019t have the ability to play against them yourself) and pay close attention to the way they play, especially when they make decisions that seem strange to you. Look at top-tier deck lists, proxy them, and play with them to figure out what makes them tick.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good, easy way to do the &quot;observe better players&quot; bit is to watch videos by MtG YouTubers. The ones playing MtG: Arena are convenient for this, since you can watch everything as it happens.<br /> <br /> I follow guys like Merchant, ThyrixSyx, Noxious, MegaMogwai, and Day[9]. Great people, very skilled, you'll learn a great deal about MtG strategy just from watching them play and explain their strategies. They have hundreds of hours of videos. It's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T14:35:30-07:00","id":1327069,"title":"","content":"Really not that excited by the new plane, and sort of frustrated with how new worlds are created and then immediately discarded. I don\u2019t know why WotC put so much effort in these settings that they toss in the trash right after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T18:05:50-07:00","id":1327099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1327069#post1327069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really not that excited by the new plane, and sort of frustrated with how new worlds are created and then immediately discarded. I don\u2019t know why WotC put so much effort in these settings that they toss in the trash right after.</div> </div> </div> </div>They return to the planes featured in the most popular sets fairly often. They\u2019ve been to Ravnica, what, three times, or four? Mirrodin, Innistrad, and Zendikar each twice. They\u2019ve been back to Dominaria twice after they started doing this plane-hopping. And they reference previously-visited planes all the time in the setting-agnostic products.<br /> <br /> What aren\u2019t you liking about this new set?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T16:27:06-07:00","id":1328826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1198398-the-mtg-thread?p=1326286#post1326286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know a way to git gud at this game that isn't boring and I can do while doing chores and stuff? As those who say my post in the You Know What I Hate Thread know, I suck at this game despite playing for years and it's less effort to just get good enough to win ocassionally without a mana-screwed opponent than to sell off all my cards and find a new way to spend my weekends.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you can't really do it during chores, I will admit that playing Arena has been great for improving my skill. Just being able to grind with zero pressure and on my own time, as well as the computer illustrating and enforcing complex stack interactions, and being able to try out/tweak different strategies without investing money, has made me a demonstrably better player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T16:39:25-07:00","id":1330855,"title":"","content":"Normally I don't do this &quot;hey, check this out!&quot; stuff. But after seeing this, I just had to share.<br /> <br /> It's an Arena video by CovertGoBlue, showing what he describes as a &quot;Golgari Prison Land Destruction&quot; deck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/O3-jBjCf4KQ\" data-code=\"O3-jBjCf4KQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/O3-jBjCf4KQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The first game is just &quot;meh&quot;, nothing special.<br /> <br /> The second game is a non-stop roller coaster. A constant back and forth, as two Control players try to out-Control each other. It's totally classic MtG.<br /> <br /> And the third game is just...it's hilarious and heart-breaking at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> That poor mono-Red player. He simply could not stop frenzying, to no effect. I felt so sorry for him.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.th